    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green. The project's only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the others under `acceptance/` are the abstract base and a log-capture helper), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners, computed from an optional `birthDate` against the owner's `registrationDate`. Because the app generates its DTOs from the OpenAPI spec and maps them with MapStruct, the change spans the spec, model, mapper, and DB schema \u2014 no controller change was needed since the existing create flow already maps input fields and sets `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` (input) schema.\n   - Added `ageBand` as a read-only enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` (output) schema.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", \u2026)` and an `ageBand(owner)` method: `MINOR` when the age at `registrationDate` is under 18, `ADULT` for 18\u201364, `SENIOR` for 65+; returns `null` when no `birthDate` is set (falling back to the current date only if `registrationDate` is somehow absent). `birthDate` itself maps straight through in both directions by name.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a nullable `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe acceptance test posts an owner with `birthDate` `1990-01-01`; measured against the create-time `registrationDate` (2026), that yields `ADULT`, which the test asserts. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
